# Known findings, ignored by exact fingerprint. Read with .github/gitleaks.toml,
# which explains why the exceptions are split between that file's path
# allowlists and this one: gitleaks 8.28.0 silently ignores `targetRules`, so an
# allowlist cannot be scoped to a single rule. Anything that has to stay live
# for one rule while being suppressed for another has to come here instead.
#
# ci.yml passes this file explicitly with --gitleaks-ignore-path, because it
# does not live at the repository root where gitleaks looks by default.
#
# Format: <commit>:<path>:<rule-id>:<line>. A fingerprint pins one finding in
# one commit. If history is ever rewritten these stop matching and the job goes
# red - which is the correct failure, because it means the scan no longer knows
# which findings were the reviewed ones.

